        "thesis": "No trade. Verified facts only: the USDJPY MT5 contract is identity-verified as a CFD with swap_long +8.275 / swap_short -17.068 and a stale quote history flag (89cdded9b2cab1ac); the current quote 157.981/158.097 at 2026-10-18 21:13 UTC is the only fresh data point. Dated macro context: DEXJPUS 158.34 on Oct 9 (79df54c8a69ce454), Fed target 3.75-4.00% held flat through Oct 18 (2156b397037e91f8, 2d1080d002a0ebd7), the dollar index up 2.87% over twenty sessions to 121.60 (c3c41aac4285fe9c), and an energy shock with Brent at 126.55 and WTI at 101.91 on Oct 14 (4cbcf0a37392f659). A plausible long-USD mechanism exists (US restrictive rates plus energy-driven terms-of-trade support for the dollar versus an energy-importing Japan), but the BoJ leg is unread: both BoJ items (c0a12ec3ec5d7b67 September MPM guideline change; 5623a36aaaccfcdc July minutes) are feed excerpts with no policy content. Without the BoJ stance, carry is unverifiable in direction and magnitude beyond broker swap metadata, which is an estimate, not a measured cost. The economic objections in the prior deferrals - undecomposed 2y-over-funds gap, no OIS strip, no consensus, no positioning - apply identically to USDJPY and are not resolved by the fresh price, since new pricing resolves only pricing objections. The GBPUSD and TLT watches show the desk has no USDJPY file at all; opening one now from macro headlines alone would be the prohibited headline-to-buy shortcut.",
        "countercase": "The strongest case against hold: the dollar index has grinded 2.87% higher over twenty sessions (c3c41aac4285fe9c) while Brent sits above 126 (4cbcf0a37392f659), and USDJPY long carries positively (swap_long +8.275), so a long-USD momentum-plus-carry trade has a defined, evidenced mechanism even without BoJ text. Technically the pair trades just under the EMA10 at 158.08 with MACD above signal, consistent with continuation. The reply: momentum and positive swap metadata are not a thesis - the desk has repeatedly rejected carry metadata as a measured cost, the BoJ September guideline change (c0a12ec3ec5d7b67) could be a policy-normalization step that would break the mechanism precisely where it is weakest, the six-hour minimum hold across weekend-to-Tokyo rollover with unmeasured spread behavior at Monday open is a real uncosted risk, and IWM/HY breadth deterioration (4fad667b9f3835a1) shows the same shared tightening factor that could flip to haven-yen flows without warning. The countercase becomes actionable only if a readable BoJ decision, an OIS strip, and measured open spreads arrive together.",
        "invalidation": "Of the hold: a readable Bank of Japan policy release confirming continued yield suppression or explicit yen-weakening tolerance, combined with fresh US prints showing labour resilience (ICSA near 199k, 8b7b5a4cbdb7a8ed) and no haven-flow regime shift, would establish the long-USDJPY mechanism on verified text and could justify a sized demo entry with the deterministic 2-ATR stop. Conversely, a BoJ hike or guideline tightening above current levels invalidates the long mechanism; verified haven flows or a volatility regime shift would override the rate-differential channel entirely, matching the desk's GBPUSD invalidation logic.",
